**Decisions the request did not spell out**
- Validation order: parsing happens first for all four bounds, then the inversion checks. So an unparseable value yields `TypeError` even though `NaN` would also look inverted; that precedence is pinned by the last test.
- The `TypeError`/`RangeError` messages name which of the four bounds failed (e.g. `end of first range is before its start: … < …`), so failures are diagnosable without a debugger.
- On the branch: there was no other branch in play, so I committed to `work/main` where the working tree already was.

